{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T17:17:27.931Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4b084a2f74dd44054f4b141a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-jbplbq"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A history line that is valid JSON but not an object (null, a number, an array) crashes pm activity and pm context with unknown_error"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found while addressing a CodeRabbit finding on PR #1761. The shared history decoder (decodeHistorySnapshot in src/core/history/read.ts) pushes any JSON value per line as a HistoryEntry, so a line such as null reaches readers that dereference entry.ts. Reproduced against the released 2026.11.20 build: append the line null to one history stream, then pm activity --limit 3 --json and pm context --for orient --json both exit 1 with code unknown_error and detail \"Cannot read properties of null (reading 'ts')\". It is the same class as pm-sew1dj, a released crash on a malformed history value. The recovery is not obvious either: pm history-repair --salvage-tail refuses non-object lines with history_salvage_refused (\"would conceal interior corruption or a malformed record\"), so the error must name a recovery that actually works (pm restore, or an explicit repair) and the advised command must be executed in a spec. Before tightening the shared decoder, census every reader of it (history, restore, verify, compaction, redaction, provenance, activity, context, stats) and the readers with their own parsers (drift-scan, health, history-storage-stats), since some may tolerate or diagnose such lines today. PR #1761 only stops the derived stream summary from adding a crash of its own (non-object entries count as irregular)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["crash","history","robustness"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-20T17:17:27.931Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T17:17:27.931Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Every command reading a history stream with a non-object JSON line refuses with a typed, documented error naming the item and the line, never unknown_error; The refusal's recovery step is executed in a spec and leaves a readable stream; A census of history readers is recorded, and readers that diagnose such lines today (health, verify) keep that behaviour"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A typed refusal naming the stream, the line and a recovery that works"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"unknown_error: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'ts') from pm activity and pm context"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"ae873518de026fd8b10523720b47087837b6b94b907096dcd8da038ff9875bdb","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"3ff95e4b9ecfa95742b13c573b3a954063760b48352e972c702196538d177ffd"}
